fg:Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Masaryk_Memorial_Cancer_Institute a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Masaryk Memorial Cancer Institute";
  dc:description "Masaryk Memorial Cancer Institute";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ror.org/0270ceh40> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Bank_of_Biological_Material,_Masaryk_Memorial_Cancer_Institute>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Bank of Biological Material, Masaryk Memorial Cancer Institute";
  dc:description "Biobank at MMCI was established to preserve patient-derived specimens such as tumours and blood-derived samples . Its structure comprises of a \"long-term storage repository\" designed to store a comprehensive set of patient samples such as tumours, adjacent tissues, genomic DNA and serum at surgery, and the \"short term storage repository\" designed to store serum aliquots from periodic determination of soluble blood tumour markers.  Comprehensive clinical data are available through the hospital infromation system to enable further translational and clinical research.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.43BD-95E2-5ED4> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Medical_data_repository_of_Institute_of_Computer_Science,_Masaryk_University>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Medical data repository of Institute of Computer Science, Masaryk University";
  dc:description "Medical research data repositories hosted by Institute of Computer Science at Masaryk University.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.BE90-1C99-5787> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Bank_of_Biological_Material,_Charles_University_-_Hradec_Králové>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Bank of Biological Material, Charles University - Hradec Králové";
  dc:description "Biobank at the Charles University Faculty of Medicine in Hradec Kralove (bbmri-eric:ID:CZ_CUNI_HK) was established at The Fingerland Department of Pathology. Majority of patients from whom the specimens are stored fall into one of the following categories: colorectal cancer, breast cancer, ovarian cancer, head&neck cancer, lung cancer, brain tumors. The tumor tissue is cryopreserved at the moment of operation for future analysis of both DNA and RNA. Formalin-fixed and paraffin embedded tissue of corresponding neoplasms is stored as well. The specimens are collected in close cooperation with clinical specialists (surgeons, oncologists, etc.).";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.130A-C3B1-7EBE> .

fg:Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_CELSPAC_Biobank a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "CELSPAC Biobank";
  dc:description "The CELSPAC Biobank started operating in 2020 as part of the RECETOX infrastructure (Masaryk University). The fully automated CELSPAC Biobank is primarily responsible for the processing and systematic storage of biological materials from CELSPAC population studies, which provide the objective information necessary to assess the association between exposure and various health outcomes. Our epidemiological databases are specifically designed to enable data sharing to promote multidisciplinary research on EXPOSOME factors that may affect human health.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.5e45-13e2-d62d> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Bank_of_Biological_Material,_Charles_University_-_Pilsen>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Bank of Biological Material, Charles University - Pilsen";
  dc:description "The Bank of Biological Material (BBM) of the Faculty of Medicine in Plzeň of Charles University has been established in the premises of the Department of Immunochemical Diagnostics of the University Hospital Plzeň. Currently the Biobank is systematically collecting for long term storage serum and plasma samples from patients with oncological diagnosis.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.73D3-2724-17D4> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Biobank_of_Institute_of_Hematology_and_Blood_Transfusion,_Prague>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Biobank of Institute of Hematology and Blood Transfusion, Prague";
  dc:description "The Biobank IHBT Prague is focused on collecting the samples of patients with haematological disorders. The samples are processed based on our SOPs and according to the type of biological material and diagnosis. Stored samples are intended for the projects approved by the Expert board of the Biobank IHBT Prague. The biobank is equipped with two automated storage systems ASKION C-line® allowing to store samples in the cryogenic temperatures at down to -185°C. For sample processing and freezing serves the ASKION C-line® work bench.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.178d-c19e-ea9b> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Bank_of_Biological_Material,_Palacký_University>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Bank of Biological Material, Palacký University";
  dc:description "The biobank affiliated with University Palacky Olomouc and University Hostpital Olomouc, focused primarily on colorectal carcinoma, lung carcinoma, glioma, prostate carcinoma, and melanoms.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.67BC-90EA-01CF> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Bank_of_Biological_Material,_Institute_of_Rheumatology>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Bank of Biological Material, Institute of Rheumatology";
  dc:description "The Bank of Biological Material of Institute of Rheumatology in Prague stores biospecimen from nearly 8 000 people and about 50 000 unique collection events covering both affected and healthy people.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.67F6-8F28-56B6> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_Bank_of_Biological_Material_of_the_First_Faculty_of_Medicine_of_Charles_University,_Prague>
  a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_000688>;
  rdfs:label "Bank of Biological Material of the First Faculty of Medicine of Charles University, Prague";
  dc:description "The Bank of Biological Material (BBM) of the First Faculty of Medicine of Charles University, Prague is primarily focused on the collection of tumour samples for future cancer research. The BBM collects samples of various types of tissues (tumour, metastases, non-tumour) classified by diagnosis, usually together with blood, serum, plasma, genomic DNA and/or urine samples taken at the time of surgery.";
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://hdl.handle.net/21.12110/1.FCFE-CA7A-A585> .

<https://w3id.org/fair-genomes/ontology/Imaging_study_Affiliated_institution_NoInformation_(NI,_nullflavor)>
